# rm230, the blunt awl (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm230
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_liv_cinderby
written_by codex
title the blunt awl
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk closes_one_eye_to_sight_a_straight_seam
likes smoked_eel wrestling festival_bells frosty_mornings
dislikes smoke wet_floors
fears an_unnoticed_split
hopes a_piece_that_wears_evenly
topics work +0.6 weather +0.4 pastimes +0.2 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=mend gossip=spare refuse=sharp tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sights along seams from one end with an eye shut, and looks just as hard at a promise, a complaint or a careless apology.

words
oath! = Hide on backwards | Three blunt awls
saying! = Judge a seam from both ends | Mark twice before making holes
seam = the joined edges | a long straight seam
awl = my short awl | the piercing tool
split = a narrow split | a shallow tear
welt = a little welt | the raised edge
cord = a waxed length | a strand of cord
hoop = a hoop of leather | a stiff ring
scrap = a piece from the trimmings | a soft offcut
edge = a shaved edge | the bevel
strain = a steady pull | a sideways strain
eel = a ribbon of smoky eel | the salty end
frost = a white crust | a prickling of frost
heel = the back of a boot | a rounded boot heel

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : A House seal takes half a second to press. Who had to stand about waiting for it to cool?
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : If I'm paying for stout goods I want the weak places pointed out first.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A torn coat doesn't have to prove deserving before somebody puts a stitch in it.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Take the bread if you need it. Nobody's entitled to count the ribs under your coat.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Music I can stand. Slippery footing and an elbow in my ear spoil a fine tune.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : When a thing breaks in the low streets, somebody nearby knows what can be salvaged.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Show me where blame joins proof. Too often there's a gap where the seam should be.

grown
line @1 greet : Stand clear of the light across this edge. There, now I can see you. | A step to the side and we're both comfortable.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : I let a stranger take the measure of me square on. | You can speak plain here without dressing it up.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Good slant to the light this early. Looks honest. | Up already. That's one thing we've got in common.
line @1 greet.return : I did hear you. I wanted to finish looking first. | Caught your voice as you came abreast of me.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your eye's as welcome as your face. Come look. | There's one wolf I can talk quite straight to.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Hello in return. I'll finish the fine work by daylight. | Too dark to do much more than talk, anyway.
line @4 greet.return [self.working=yes] : You can speak while I'm working. I don't need my ears for this join. | A greeting doesn't put me behind. Hello.
line @1 again.open : We keep coming level with each other. | You've only missed one bit of progress.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A straight answer for kin. Come get it. | There you are. Stand by my better side.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Over here where the light runs along the edge. | If you've a minute I'd value your eye.
line @1 farewell : Go carefully where the footing changes. | Take your time with the uneven part.
line @1 farewell.return : And to you. I'll see this bit through. | Leave the light where I can use it.
line @1 react.news : Lead with whatever you witnessed personally. | Give it a clean edge for me.
line @1 react.news.known : That matches the first account near enough. | I'd heard it laid out almost exactly so.
line @1 react.news.new : First I've known of any such thing. | There's a join in the tale I hadn't seen.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That won't bear any weight till you've got more to go on. | I find a weak place in that story every time.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|theft|assault|arrest|crime|loss] : You can count on me for the practical part. | Damnably hard news. I'll give you my full attention.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|work|birth|apprentice] : Yes, that's something that'll hold up under a bit of wear. | A good strong piece of news for once.
line @1 ask.how : Where does the day sit badly on you? | Holding up under today's pull?
line @1 answer.how : My patience is wearing at the corners. Otherwise sound. | I'm as level as the work permits.
line @1 decline : I'd make a promise I couldn't carry through. I won't do it. | Ask for something smaller and I may have a different answer.
line @1 accept_decline : Clean refusal. Leaves me sure where I stand. | Better now than halfway through the job.
line @1 preclose : I'd like the light for a last inspection. | I'll go before fatigue makes a sloppy job of me.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. We came to a clean stopping place. | You've done your share of the listening.
line @1 thank : You showed me the weak point before I leaned on it. Thanks. | I know what that took. I'm obliged to you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : A straight join's worth the time it takes. | I'd have bothered if nobody was looking.
line @1 sympathise : I believe you about the part nobody can see. | It wears through underneath sometimes. That's still a hurt.
line @1 reassure : Let's see what's solid before we start counting splits. | One good patch buys the time for a better mend.
line @1 ack : Straight enough for me. | Yes, those ends meet.
scene closing_eye
when topic=work|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I shut one eye to look for a crooked join. | Turn the work end for end before you call it straight.
b : Wouldn't two eyes see more? | The join won't change.
a : More, yes. I want one answer to one question. | Your eye might. It gets fond of a line it drew itself.

scene small_split
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Holes set close together aren't always a kindness to the stuff between. | I won't drive an awl through till I know where it comes out.
b : More stitches should hold better. | Surely it's the other side?
a : Enough little holes make one fine long tear. | That's a side. I asked for a place. There's a difference.

scene tight_cord
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave a touch of play in this cord. | A beautiful tight stitch can be a miserable thing to wear.
b : Afraid it'll snap? | You look proud of it all the same.
a : Of the cord cutting the edge before it ever thinks of snapping. | I'm looking to see where I ought to loosen it.

scene rain_margin
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Never mind the clouds. Look at the dark edge of that patch of paving. | The last drop to fall from an eave is the one I wait for.
b : What will it tell you? | Why that one?
a : If the wet edge stops moving, the water's easing up. | Because I forgot it once and went out with a clean collar.

scene look_frost
when topic=weather here.weather=clear here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Frost prints every scratch on a flat stone. | White crust on a rail shows where a warm paw rested.
b : You can read scratches now? | Reading tracks on a railing?
a : Only how deep they lie. The story's somebody else's affair. | No. Just pleased to see a little warmth made a mark.

scene dark_supper
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I separate the flesh from an eel in a single strip if it'll let me. | Smoke on a slice of eel is one thing. Smoke up my nose is quite another.
b : Does it always oblige? | Which end are you standing at?
a : No, and the little pieces taste exactly as good. | The supper end, for preference. Leave the stinging eyes to somebody else.

scene shoulder_hold
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good wrestler feels the slack before making a pull. | Nobody wins a fair hold by worrying the fur.
b : Sounds like work. | Does pulling fur happen often?
a : That bit does. The happy landing is what makes it a pastime. | Once is plenty. I make my feelings plain before there's a second.

scene two_bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll have the bells without the crush of the square, thank you. | Bells carry farther than the folk selling things under them.
b : Where would you stand? | That's the attraction?
a : Just off the main way. Same sound, better use of my ribs. | A tune I can enjoy without anyone trying to wrap it up and price it.

scene headroom
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A Sump stair can wear its edge down on just one side. | I can tell the busy half of a landing by the smooth boards.
b : Same feet over and over? | Which half would you choose?
a : Usually. Most of us have learned where the wall can lend a shoulder. | The rough. Better hold underfoot when a crowd comes through.

scene honest_cut
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give more for one square scrap than two you can't match. | Price the part you can use. The scraps aren't much of a bargain.
b : Because it's prettier? | Not the time spent?
a : Because I know exactly what I can get out of it. | Count the time. Just don't ask me to pay for the trimmings twice.

scene heavy_shift
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : In a lean spell I see more patches sewn over other patches. | A bad week makes things wear through faster.
b : Does the third one even hold? | Same amount of wear, surely.
a : Only as well as what's still underneath. And that's the worry. | Yes. Fewer things to spread it over.

scene needle_rumour
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've heard talk with a point at both ends. Very little use for it. | Stories told sideways tend to stick.
b : Why not? | Stick where?
a : Whoever takes hold gets pricked. That seems a poor piece of work. | To the least deserving nose, usually. I'm keeping mine clear.

scene fog_register
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Can't sight a straight line very far in this fog. | Fog makes a wall seem nearer if you're impatient.
b : What do you use instead? | You've tried that, haven't you.
a : My front paw. Slow business, but honest. | Nearly did. Pride would look poor with a flat nose.

scene borrowed_corner
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# an unfinished piece. That's my measure of trust. | I value the quiet I can have beside #self.friend#.
b : Worried somebody might steal the idea? | Nothing to say?
a : No. A verdict on a single unfinished hem does the coat little justice. | Plenty. A friend doesn't require it all at once.

scene loose_grain
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A scratch across an edge catches my eye even at a distance. | I will quite often go back to look at something twice.
b : Hard to leave it alone? | Always find a fault?
a : Looking is allowed. Touching somebody else's work is another question. | Sometimes I see how very well it was done. That's worth the walk back.

scene bothends
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My kind of prayer begins with looking and ends with doing. | A blessing on a poor mend is a nice thought. I'd still like it mended.
b : Looking for what? | You ask for quite a bit.
a : Whoever needs the spare seat. No sense offering a chair to a door. | Just the whole job. Good wishes take up very little room beside it.

scene night_eye
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : By lamplight I trust the pad of a finger first. | A shadow can put a kink into a perfectly straight line.
b : Do you feel a flaw that small? | How do you check it?
a : I can feel where I need to stop and look again in daylight. | Move the lamp. If the kink moves too we've saved a lot of needless poking.

scene finished_test
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I'd like to make something that wears out evenly everywhere at once. | Imagine a pair of boots with no weak corner.
b : Then nobody could patch it. | You'd still have to wear them out.
a : No, but nobody would curse a single rotten seam either. | Happily. Every scuff would be fair wear. That's a decent aim.

story crooked_belt [topic=memories|work self.job=crafter]
  : I once laid a long piece along a rail to get the join ruler-straight. Very handsome thing when I took it off.
  : The rail had been bowed in the middle. So had my handsome piece.
  b : Was the whole piece wasted?
  : Found something round that wanted binding. Let the rail have its one little victory.

story wrestling_eyes [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I used to close one eye on a wrestling hold the way I would on a seam. Want to know what I overlooked?
  : The whole other side of the wrestler. Hit the ground quite pleased at having spotted the mistake.
  b : Did you get back up?
  : With both eyes wide. Made an appreciable difference.

story odd_scrap [topic=home|memories]
  : I kept a trimming cut in the curl of a tail. Never could find anything that wanted such an extraordinary patch.
  : One day a pot began rocking on the sill. Slid the tail under the low foot and there the thing stayed.
  b : Does that count as a mend?
  : Pot's still whole. Foot's still low. Call it an agreement.

rule @wetfloor
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Short steps on that shine. It doesn't give much grip. | Dark at the join means wet underfoot.

rule @craft
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave me a sound margin beside that cut! | If the edges creep, stop and bring them back level.

rule @eyes
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give me the view from the far end a minute. | I want that line where the light strikes along it.

rule @meal
when concept=bark self.likes=smoked_eel
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Skin off, sweet strip in the middle. That's the bite I want. | Leave the narrow end. It has a good chew to it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : If it's a plain question there's no need to come at it sideways.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I recognise the way you stand just clear of the work.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Waiting till daylight for a close look. I can give you an ear.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep your paws well clear while you ask that.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=crafter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I want anything that leaves my bench to bear a decent pull.
dlg @2 resident.job : Useful work. Looking twice is part of finishing.
dlg @1 resident.bye : That'll hold us till we speak again.
graft resident.hub
choice Why look at a seam with one eye shut? -> seam_sight
node seam_sight
say I want the line against one fixed point. I walk my eye along it from both ends. A bad stitch is a little hill in otherwise level country.
free
choice What if you only find one bad stitch? -> badstitch
choice I'll leave you the light. -> hub
node badstitch
say Pull on each side of it. If the neighbours take the strain, it can stay. I mind what holds up better than what looks perfect.
choice That's a useful test. -> hub
choice I'm off now. -> bye
